      "type": "text",
      "text": "I've marked execution as UNKNOWN, not NORMAL: growth needs a tube pressure reading and this furnace has no pressure gauge, so I can't confirm the atmosphere.\n\n- **Other sensors look fine.** Temperature briefly overshot to 760.5 °C when growth started, then settled at 750.0 °C, which is the setpoint. Heater power is steady at about 46%. Argon flow is about 100 sccm, as set. Exhaust oxygen dropped to about 6 ppm during the purge and has stayed at 5–8 ppm since.\n- **What the gap hides.** Low oxygen argues against a leak letting air in. But a blocked exhaust would mainly show up as rising pressure, and nothing installed can detect that.\n- **Science.** No characterization of the sample exists yet, so there's no evidence about whether the material grew.\n\nMy recommended action is to call a human to check the exhaust line or bubbler, or to add a pressure measurement."
     }
